      <Xref identifier="Q6K2Y8" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1042.463134765625" centerY="690.538330078125" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi, O-27, pujar">Searching a cDNA library prepared from Fe-deficient rice roots using the barley NAAT genes as probes identified four rice NAAT genes. Database searches using sequence from the four genes identified two additional genes. The six genes were named NAAT1-6 |CITS: [18034312]|. Among the six genes, |FRAME: G-10643 NAAT1| was the most similar to the barley genes - 76% homologous to |FRAME: G-10647 naatA| and 74% to |FRAME: G-10649 naatB|. Northern blot and QPCR analyses has shown that only |FRAME: G-10643 NAAT1| was strongly induced under Fe deficiency, while the other genes were expressed constitutively. Thus |FRAME: G-10643 NAAT1| was chosen for further characterization |CITS: [18034312]|. The |FRAME: G-10643 NAAT1| gene was cloned as a fusion with maltose-binding protein and expressed in |FRAME: TAX-562 &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;|, and the recombinant protein was purified. An enzyme assay conducted with the purified protein verified its activity |CITS: [18034312]|. The localization of |FRAME: G-10643 NAAT1| expression in both Fe-sufficient and Fe-deficient rice plants was investigated by using a NAAT1 promoter-GUS fusion transformants. In roots of Fe-deficient plants the promoter activity was much stronger than in Fe-defficient plants, and was detected in all tissues, including the epidermis, exodermis, cortex and whole stele. Strong signal was also detected in all vascular bundles and mesophyll cells in chlorotic young leaves of Fe-deficient plants |CITS: [18034312]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-13941" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phytozome" value="Os02t0306401-00" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR005958" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF00155" />
